@anon.9efbc0c128adab6190fabe7f7e045142.862 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1026 x i8] }> <{ [1026 x i8] c"Reads structured data from a YAML file.\0A\0AThe file must contain a valid YAML object or array. YAML mappings will be\0Aconverted into Typst dictionaries, and YAML sequences will be converted into\0ATypst arrays. Strings and booleans will be converted into the Typst\0Aequivalents, null-values (`null`, `~` or empty ``) will be converted into\0A`{none}`, and numbers will be converted to floats or integers depending on\0Awhether they are whole numbers. Custom YAML tags are ignored, though the\0Aloaded value will still be present.\0A\0ABe aware that integers larger than 2<sup>63</sup>-1 will be converted to\0Afloating point numbers, which may give an approximative value.\0A\0AThe YAML files in the example contain objects with authors as keys,\0Aeach with a sequence of their own submapping with the keys\0A\22title\22 and \22published\22\0A\0A# Example\0A```example\0A#let bookshelf(contents) = {\0A  for (author, works) in contents {\0A    author\0A    for work in works [\0A      - #work.title (#work.published)\0A    ]\0A  }\0A}\0A\0A#bookshelf(\0A  yaml(\22scifi-authors.yaml\22)\0A)\0A```" }>, align 1
